From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qwen3.8: fp8 copy of lm_head for MTP draft logits

VLLM_QWEN38_DRAFT_HEAD_FP8 (default 0 = unchanged). The MTP drafter reads its
draft logits from a per-row e4m3 copy of the shared lm_head through Marlin
W8A16 instead of the BF16 head: 248320 x 2560, 0.45 ms instead of 0.77 ms per
draft step at one row on CMP 170HX, three draft steps per decode step. Target
verification keeps the BF16 head, so the output distribution is unchanged;
only draft quality (acceptance) can move. Built in MTPSpeculator.load_draft_model
on the stage that hosts the head, before CUDA-graph capture (+0.59 GiB). TP=1.
